### Top Concerns about overuse of AI
@(0.7,0.9) `ofria.com/Talks/AI`
...
- AI-facilitated plagiarism or dishonesty
...
- Reduction in critical thinking / creativity / engagement
...
- Increasing Isolation
...
- De-skilling:
@(469, 295) {w=800px} ![image](data:image/jpeg;base64,)
@(490, 296) {size=18px} [https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(25)02075-6](https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(25)02075-6)
---
### Effects of AI on CS enrollment
...
Overall **undergraduate enrollment** increased 1.3% in 2026{{br}}{{size=18px|[](https://nscresearchcenter.org/enrollment-insights/)}}
...
In 2025, **CS bachelor’s degrees** reached a peak of 41,858, but new majors fell to 33,490, a 13% drop year-over-year. {{br}}{{size=18px|[](https://cra.org/crn/category/2026/vol-38-no-6/)}}
...
**CS job openings** are down 25% since Feb 2020, but up 15% since Feb 2025. 71% of increase are senior roles; 37% mention AI in title. {{br}}{{size=18px|[](https://hiringlab.indeed.com/2026/07/08/ai-and-job-postings-from-destruction-to-creation/)}}
...
U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics has a rosy **projection for CS jobs** : 16% growth in software developer, but a 6% drop in computer programmer {{br}}{{size=18px|[](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm)}}
---
### Most Universities are Reacting, often BIG
...
**[UIC](https://today.uic.edu/uic-engineering-launches-ai-curriculum-initiatives)** – AI-from day one in CS for non-majors, AI integration for CS majors, discipline-specific for other STEM.
...
**[U. Victoria](https://news.uvic.ca/2026/teaching-tomorrow-why-uvic-computer-science-redesigned-its-degree)** – AI explicitly woven into all courses in curriculum (started in 2023)
...
**[UW–Madison](https://cai.wisc.edu/about/faqs/)** – New college of “Computing and AI”
...
**[Ohio State](https://oaa.osu.edu/ai-fluency)** - Requirement of AI fluence for all majors
...
**[U. Michigan](https://its.umich.edu/computing/ai/canvas-maizey-integration)** - Supplies AI tools to instructors as digital TAs (Maizey).
...
**[U. Notre Dame](https://honorcode.nd.edu/generative-ai-policy-for-students-august-2023)** AI is prohibited by default; instructors can override prohibition.
---
### How do we update OUR learning outcomes?
...
What do students need to still be able to do, unaided by AI?
...
{size=24px} - Most CS fundamentals (e.g., theory)
...
{size=24px} - Low-level coding
...
{size=24px} - Testing frameworks
...
What outcomes do we want to elevate having to do with AI?
...
{size=24px} - Reading / diagnosing code
...
{size=24px} - Clear requirements specification
...
{size=24px} - Higher expectations in class projects that use AI
...
What topics can we deemphasize?
...
{size=24px} - Web development? App development?
...
{size=24px} - ???
...
{color=white, thick=4, textcolor=#ccffcc, fill=black, size=44} !textbox (0.2, 0.3) (0.6, 0.4) For this to work, we need to{{br}}ensure that of our students{{br}}have access to quality AI!
---
### How do we stop students from outsourcing learning to AI?
...
- In a 2023-24 Cornell study of 95,513 students, 9% of students admit to cheating with AI (26% of who use AI daily admitted cheating)
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[](https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aec5115)
...
- In the 2026 HEPI survey of 1,054 UK undergraduates, **94% used generative AI in connection with assessed work**
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[](https://www.hepi.ac.uk/reports/student-generative-ai-survey-2026)
...
- GPT use improved math scores by **48%** for HS students; they later did **17% worse** than controls when unassisted. (A custom AI tutor improved assisted performance by **127%** and no different from controls when unassisted).
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[](https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2422633122)
---
### Evaluation Techniques
...
- More in-class quizzes / exams
...
- Flipped classrooms (coding done in front of instructors)
...
- Project presentations
...
- AI-generated personalized quizzes on student’s own projects
...
- More programming labs associated with courses
...
- A department (or college) testing center
---
### How do we use AI in teaching?
...
- Like an army of competent TAs who are terrible at holding back information from the students?
...
- Custom quizzes and exams?
...
- If we get our own AI server: answer course specific questions WITHOUT giving away the full solution.
---
### How do we handle continued AI advances?
...
- New ongoing committee to focus on AI plans and policies
...
- Develop more ties to industry, especially in AI
...
- Ensure student access to current AI systems?
---
### MITs Eight Guiding Principles for AI
MIT released a [report](https://aiandeducation.mit.edu/report/) with recommendations including the principles:
...
- Be Humble
- Be Bold
- Put Humanity Front and Center
- Lean into Learning
- Teach with Intentionality
- No One Size Fits All
- Augmentation not Automation
- Think Beyond the Classroom and the Campus
...
{color=white, thick=4, textcolor=#ffcccc, fill=black, size=44} !textbox (0.2, 0.3) (0.6, 0.4) TLDR: This is an important challenge.{{br}}{{br}}Good luck!
